From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 11] i915: display on Ivy Bridge only

The illumos build carries i915's display code for Ivy Bridge (display
version 7), the only display hardware it has been tested on (ThinkPad
X230); the families it leaves out (DSI, HDCP, LPE audio) and the
stubs replacing them are checked against that platform's paths
(illumos/gen-nodisplay.py --excluded). On every other platform
intel_display_device_probe() takes Linux's no_display path, as for a
device ID without display, and says so at info level: the display
structure then has the empty device info, HAS_DISPLAY() is false, and
intel_display_device_info_runtime_init() clears DRIVER_MODESET and
DRIVER_ATOMIC from the device's features, so that the DRM core starts no
mode setting for it (drm_dev_illumos_lkms_register() does nothing) and
the interrupt setup takes the headless registers of patch 0006.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_device.c
@@ -1707,8 +1707,24 @@
 		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
 			    "Unknown device ID %04x; disabling display.\n",
 			    pdev->device);
+		goto no_display;
+	}
+
+#ifdef __illumos__
+	/*
+	 * illumos drives the display of Ivy Bridge only (the hardware it
+	 * was tested on); every other platform keeps the headless
+	 * behaviour of Linux's no_display description, which also clears
+	 * DRIVER_MODESET and DRIVER_ATOMIC in
+	 * intel_display_device_info_runtime_init().
+	 */
+	if (!desc->platforms.ivybridge) {
+		drm_info(display->drm,
+			 "display on %s is not supported on illumos; running headless\n",
+			 desc->name);
 		goto no_display;
 	}
+#endif
 
 	info = desc->info;
 	if (!info)
